sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Engineer
    participant Host as Available coding-agent host
    participant State as Task state / source lock
    participant Primary as DevSecOps primary
    participant Sec as AI Agent Security
    participant AI as AI Native
    participant Ops as DevOps
    participant QA as QA
    participant SCM as GitHub / CI
    participant Human as Named human approver
    participant Runtime as Production runtime / operations

    Engineer->>Host: Open trusted workspace and select available host
    Host->>State: Recover goal, requirements, SHA and first unmet gate
    State-->>Host: Scope, evidence, constraints and acceptance
    Host->>Host: Verify effective tools, permissions and session capture
    Host->>Primary: Load primary four-artifact role pack
    Primary->>Primary: Discover system, baseline, threats and failure domains
    par Independent security review when needed
        Host->>Sec: Bounded agent/tool/identity threat review
        Sec-->>Primary: Attack paths, enforcement and negative tests
    and
        Host->>AI: Bounded production AI/data-flow review
        AI-->>Primary: Workload lifecycle, tenancy and evaluation risks
    end
    Host->>Ops: Assign delivery/performance/HA-DR review when needed
    Ops-->>Primary: Pipeline, identity, capacity and recovery evidence
    Primary->>Host: Options, trade-offs and bounded implementation plan
    Host->>Host: Scoped code/config/test changes
    Host->>QA: Acceptance challenge
    QA-->>Host: Functional/security/performance/resilience oracles
    Host->>SCM: Push branch / open PR
    SCM->>SCM: Run untrusted validation and required checks
    SCM->>Human: Present exact diff, checks, artifact/plan and target
    Human->>SCM: Approve named production change
    SCM->>Runtime: Protected deploy with short-lived identity
    Runtime-->>Host: Health, audit, performance and recovery evidence
    Host->>State: Persist exact revision, results, unknowns and next action
